Agar external examiner ne **"Implementation of Continuous Integration / Continuous Deployment with Jenkins and Java & Cloning in GitHub"** experiment diya hai aur aapko kuch nahi aata, to ye **sabse simple practical method** follow karo.

## Experiment ka Basic Flow

```text
Java Program
    ↓
GitHub Repository
    ↓
Git Clone
    ↓
Jenkins
    ↓
Build Java Program
    ↓
Run Program
    ↓
SUCCESS
```

---

# Step 1: Install Required Software

### 1. Install Java JDK

Check:

```cmd
java -version
javac -version
```

Agar version show ho raha hai to Java installed hai.

---

### 2. Install Git

Check:

```cmd
git --version
```

---

### 3. Install Jenkins

Download from:

[Jenkins Download Page](https://www.jenkins.io/download/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Install normally.

Browser me open karo:

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

---

# Step 2: Create Simple Java Project

Desktop par folder banao:

```text
JenkinsDemo
```

Uske andar file banao:

```text
HelloWorld.java
```

Code:

```java
public class HelloWorld {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello Jenkins CI/CD");
    }
}
```

---

# Step 3: Test Java Program

CMD open karo.

Folder me jao:

```cmd
cd Desktop\JenkinsDemo
```

Compile:

```cmd
javac HelloWorld.java
```

Run:

```cmd
java HelloWorld
```

Output:

```text
Hello Jenkins CI/CD
```

Examiner ko bolo:

> First I verified the Java application locally.

---

# Step 4: Create GitHub Repository

Open:

[GitHub](https://github.com?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

1. Sign In
2. New Repository
3. Repository Name:

```text
JenkinsDemo
```

4. Create Repository

---

# Step 5: Push Code to GitHub

Project folder me CMD:

Initialize Git:

```cmd
git init
```

Add file:

```cmd
git add .
```

Commit:

```cmd
git commit -m "Initial Commit"
```

Connect Repository:

```cmd
git remote add origin https://github.com/USERNAME/JenkinsDemo.git
```

Push:

```cmd
git push -u origin master
```

Refresh GitHub.

File upload dikh jayegi.

---

# Step 6: Cloning in GitHub

Repository URL copy karo.

Example:

```text
https://github.com/USERNAME/JenkinsDemo.git
```

New folder me clone karo:

```cmd
git clone https://github.com/USERNAME/JenkinsDemo.git
```

Output:

```text
Cloning into 'JenkinsDemo'
```

Examiner ko bolo:

> Cloning creates a local copy of a remote repository.

---

# Step 7: Open Jenkins

Browser:

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

Login.

---

# Step 8: Create Jenkins Job

1. Dashboard
2. New Item
3. Name:

```text
JavaProject
```

4. Freestyle Project
5. OK

---

# Step 9: Configure GitHub Repository

Source Code Management → Git

Paste:

```text
https://github.com/USERNAME/JenkinsDemo.git
```

---

# Step 10: Build Step Add

Build Section →

Add Build Step →

Windows:

```cmd
javac HelloWorld.java
java HelloWorld
```

---

# Step 11: Build Now

Click:

```text
Build Now
```

Left side Build History me build start hoga.

Green tick aaye to build successful.

---

# Step 12: Check Console Output

Build Number → Console Output

Output:

```text
Started by user

Cloning repository

Compiling Java Program

Running Program

Hello Jenkins CI/CD

Finished: SUCCESS
```

